F(z) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} u[n] z^{-n}

The step-sequence u[n] is defined as:

u[n] = \begin{cases} 1, & n \geq 0 \\ 0, & n < 0 \end{cases}

So, we can rewrite the equation as:

F(z) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} z^{-n}

This is a geometric series with the first term a = 1 and the common ratio r = z^-1. The sum of an infinite geometric series is given by:

S = \frac{a}{1 - r}

In this case, a = 1 and r = z^-1, so we have:

F(z) = \frac{1}{1 - z^{-1}}

This is the Z-transform of the step-sequence f[n] = u[n].

